// Doubler.fol — package source file
// Spec: language-ref.md > Syntax 3 — Function objects
//
// The result-side companion to Handler.fol. Together they are the spec's
// `someFArg` / `someFRet` function-object pair:
//
//     Handler co.lang.function = (a co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int) = { ... }
//     Doubler co.lang.function = (a co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int) = { ... }
//
// A function object is a concrete VALUE. That is exactly why Syntax 3 cannot
// express a Rank-2 or Rank-3 polymorphic parameter — a value cannot carry a
// quantifier. Use `co.lang.type = forall(T).(T)->(T)` for those.
//
// A direct anonymous-function body ends at its closing brace and takes no
// semicolon (DECISION-SYN-007).

_ co.lang.unit = {
Doubler co.lang.function = (a co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int) {
    this.return a * 2;
};
}
